WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.458
Adding one server

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.177
should not break

00:00:02.154 --> 00:00:03.404
every cache lookup

00:00:03.942 --> 00:00:05.109
With four servers

00:00:05.239 --> 00:00:06.406
hash key modulo

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.479
N spreads keys

00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:08.022
evenly

00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:08.800
but adding a

00:00:08.612 --> 00:00:09.897
fifth server changes

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:10.687
the remainder for

00:00:10.499 --> 00:00:11.394
most keys

00:00:11.926 --> 00:00:12.716
In a test

00:00:12.527 --> 00:00:13.506
with one hundred

00:00:13.318 --> 00:00:14.579
thousand fake keys

00:00:14.685 --> 00:00:15.652
the author found

00:00:15.464 --> 00:00:16.218
that adding a

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:17.268
fifth server makes

00:00:17.115 --> 00:00:18.128
roughly four out

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.036
of five lookups

00:00:18.848 --> 00:00:19.484
miss

00:00:20.006 --> 00:00:21.185
Consistent hashing

00:00:20.997 --> 00:00:21.739
fixes it with

00:00:21.551 --> 00:00:22.116
a ring

00:00:22.364 --> 00:00:23.496
each server and

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:24.027
key gets a

00:00:23.839 --> 00:00:24.605
spot on a

00:00:24.416 --> 00:00:25.265
clock face

00:00:25.348 --> 00:00:26.020
and a new

00:00:25.831 --> 00:00:27.152
server only takes

00:00:26.964 --> 00:00:27.847
the keys next

00:00:27.659 --> 00:00:28.237
to it

00:00:28.758 --> 00:00:29.772
Full story on

00:00:29.583 --> 00:00:30.479
the dashboard
